Gold Price Prediction Using RNN, LSTM and GRU

Dataset
This project uses the Gold Price Dataset available on Kaggle:
Dataset Source - https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/rizkykiky/gold-price-dataset
The dataset contains historical gold price data provided at different time intervals, including:
Daily
Weekly
Monthly
Quarterly
Yearly
It also contains Average (Avg) and End of Period (EoP) versions for some time intervals.
For this project, we specifically use:
Daily.csv

Important Columns
Date – Date of the recorded gold price
INR – Gold price in Indian Rupees
The INR column contains values such as 6,250.50, so commas are removed and the values are converted into numerical format before training.

Data Preprocessing
The daily data is sorted chronologically and missing values are removed. The gold prices are normalized using MinMaxScaler, converting the values approximately to a range of 0 to 1.
A 30-day sliding window is then created:

Previous 30 days → Next day's gold price
The resulting data is divided chronologically into 80% training data and 20% testing data.

Models
Three recurrent neural network models are implemented and compared:
Simple RNN
LSTM
GRU
Each model uses the previous 30 days of gold prices to predict the next day's price.

Evaluation
The models are evaluated using:
MAE – Mean Absolute Error
RMSE – Root Mean Squared Error
R² – R-squared Score
The results are compared using tables and graphs to determine which model performs best for gold price prediction.
